1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:02,865
What is ONLORE Season One building?

2
00:00:03,095 --> 00:00:07,850
ONLORE connects emerging projects with creators, with gaming at its core.

3
00:00:08,080 --> 00:00:15,740
It announced a five hundred thousand dollar Echo round, backed by more than sixty-eight angel operators and Web3 creators.

4
00:00:17,225 --> 00:00:22,705
Season One offers discovery and content creation tasks that earn Season Shards after review.

5
00:00:22,935 --> 00:00:29,150
The advertised one hundred thousand dollar plus ten percent LOR prize pool is planned, not guaranteed.

6
00:00:29,380 --> 00:00:36,865
My perspective: its long-term appeal depends on playable games, transparent reviews, and meaningful creator access.

7
00:00:38,350 --> 00:00:44,785
Start with the two mandatory tasks: connect your X account, then answer the feedback questions.

8
00:00:45,015 --> 00:00:50,415
Explain what ONLORE could improve, which game you would add, and what would make you invite a friend.

9
00:00:50,645 --> 00:00:55,320
Sharing on X is optional. It does not replace the mandatory tasks.

10
00:00:56,808 --> 00:01:02,113
For a written piece, choose a question that genuinely helps a newcomer understand the project.

11
00:01:02,343 --> 00:01:08,183
Publish original work on an accepted platform, such as Medium or a public Notion page.

12
00:01:08,413 --> 00:01:14,058
A browser draft is not a published article. You need a working link that reviewers can open.

13
00:01:15,558 --> 00:01:21,673
A useful video combines an introduction, a practical explanation, and your own assessment.

14
00:01:21,903 --> 00:01:28,488
Videos under five minutes can earn up to two hundred Shards. Longer videos can earn up to three hundred and fifty.

15
00:01:28,718 --> 00:01:33,068
Those are maximum scores after review, not automatic rewards.

16
00:01:34,558 --> 00:01:40,378
After publishing, open the link in a private browser window to check that other people can view it.

17
00:01:40,608 --> 00:01:44,318
Paste it into the correct task and select the right format.

18
00:01:44,548 --> 00:01:50,543
X links are not accepted for these Create submissions. Publishing and receiving approval are separate steps.

19
00:01:52,058 --> 00:01:56,393
People review effort and quality, rather than views or likes.

20
00:01:56,623 --> 00:02:02,038
The supplied rules allow up to ten Create submissions per week, with only the best six counting.

21
00:02:02,268 --> 00:02:08,498
I would focus on fact-checking and a useful point of view, instead of posting near-identical pieces.

22
00:02:10,017 --> 00:02:16,297
The prize pool is described as planned. That is an important qualification, not a footnote to ignore.

23
00:02:16,527 --> 00:02:21,112
Season Shards are campaign points. They are not money already received.

24
00:02:21,342 --> 00:02:26,072
Check the current rules and review requirements before committing time or spending money.

25
00:02:27,558 --> 00:02:34,193
What I want to see next is playable games, transparent reviews, and meaningful access for creators.

26
00:02:34,423 --> 00:02:38,693
Would I still want to explore these projects if the leaderboard disappeared?

27
00:02:38,923 --> 00:02:43,923
Explore the project, check the details, and tell us what you would like to see next.

28
00:02:44,153 --> 00:02:47,008
Created for the ONLORE Season One campaign.
